{
  "//": [
    "The conformance matrix: one entry per feature, not per file. A row is added",
    "here and nowhere else — there is no per-case lldb script to edit.",
    "",
    "`program` is the basename under tension-core/tests/programs (build-test-programs",
    "resolves its folder and flags). `file` is the guest source the breakpoint names,",
    "which is what the debugger reports, so it must match the compiler's own DW_AT_name",
    "for that source (a basename, not a path).",
    "",
    "Group A rows carry `marker`: the runner finds the single source line holding",
    "`// @<marker>` and breaks there. Group B rows carry `transcript`: the name of the",
    "program's own print function, and every call to it becomes a case named after the",
    "feature and its position, so a red row reads `main_policy.transcript#2` rather",
    "than a raw line number."
  ],
  "cases": [
    { "group": "A", "name": "first_statement_print", "program": "first-statement", "file": "first-statement.tension", "marker": "@stop" },
    { "group": "A", "name": "first_statement_after_declarations", "program": "first-after-decls", "file": "first-after-decls.tension", "marker": "@stop" },
    { "group": "A", "name": "first_statement_branch", "program": "first-branch", "file": "first-branch.tension", "marker": "@stop" },
    { "group": "A", "name": "first_statement_loop", "program": "first-loop", "file": "first-loop.tension", "marker": "@stop" },
